PEAK HEAP ACROSS TWO ALLOCATION-SHAPE CHANGES — and one of them is a NULL.

date:   2026-09-03
host:   r7900x — AMD Ryzen 7900X, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. NOT the aarch64 box
        the RSS records use. HEAP, not RSS — a different quantity.
        The box was concurrently running a zenfleet sweep (~15 of 24 threads);
        that affects wall clock, which is NOT what this file reports, and not
        heap bytes, which are load-independent.
tool:   heaptrack + heaptrack_print ("peak heap memory consumption").
cell:   gradient <size>x<size> qp 40 preset 13, 8-bit 4:2:0, ONE encode per
        cell (not a median). Sizes 1280 / 1536 / 1920 / 2048.
arms:   still    = perf_encode default (avif still config), 1 frame
        videokey = SVTAV1_VIDEO=1, 1 frame
        inter    = SVTAV1_VIDEO=1 SVTAV1_FRAMES=2 SVTAV1_FRAME_SHIFT=3
        Every cell's `.obu` was checked non-empty before its peak was read
        (mem_heaptrack_2026-09-03.meta's refusal trap).
trees:  BASE  = de4bfaf7 (main, the tx_class monomorphisation)
        ARENA = BASE + the PA/ME pooling commit
        RESRV = ARENA + the tile-buffer reservation commit

