======================= WHAT THIS SAYS =======================

1. **THE PA/ME POOLING IS A NULL — twelve cells, identical to the digit.**
   Measured, not argued. The reason is structural and is now recorded in the
   commit: the recycle first hands back an allocation on FRAME 2, and
   `encode_frame_impl` REFUSES frame 2, so the code cannot execute through the
   public encoder at all; and even once it can, at a 2-frame peak BOTH frames'
   pyramids and result sets are simultaneously live, so recycling removes
   allocation CHURN and not live bytes.

   This corrects the prescription in `mem_heaptrack_2026-09-03.meta` ("one
   arena allocated at pipeline construction that the per-SB buffers are
   `&mut [T]` slices INTO"). That shape is right for the CHURN — 3,072 mallocs
   per frame at `MeB64Output::new` alone — and cannot by itself close the
   memory gap, because the gap is a LIFETIME property: the port holds the
   whole frame's decision tree, with a coefficient `Vec` per block, until the
   entropy walk, where C packs a superblock and releases its buffers.

2. **The tile-buffer reservation moves the INTER arm only, by 0.4-2.4 %, and
   its size is a function of how far the tile's area sits above a power of
   two.** 2048x2048 is exactly 4 MiB, so a doubling `Vec` lands on its payload
   with zero slack and the change is worth exactly nothing there; 1536x1536 is
   2.25 MiB, so the doubling reserves 4 MiB and 1.75 MiB is slack. **This is
   why the size sweep exists: a single 2048 cell would have reported the
   change as NULL, and a single 1536 cell would have reported 2.4 % as if it
   generalised.** Neither is the truth; the truth is "between 0 and 2.4 %,
   keyed on the binary expansion of the tile area".

3. The still and videokey arms do not move at all, on either change. The
   growth this reserves away is live at the INTER arm's peak and not at
   theirs.

======================= NOT ESTABLISHED =======================

  * Any RSS number. This is heap.
  * Any aarch64 number. Different allocator, different page size.
  * Repeat variance: one encode per cell.
  * Any preset other than 13, any content other than gradient, any qp but 40.
